<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>C022 tenant isolation inspector</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Can one tenant see another?</h1>
<p>Synthetic data · loopback HTTP only · every decision below is made by the server. This page only asks, with real GET requests, as a user of each of two tenants, and shows what came back. Its verdicts are computed from the facts it observed, never from server prose.</p>

<section aria-labelledby="present-title">
<h2 id="present-title">1. Present two sessions</h2>
<p>
<label for="token-a">Session token of a user of the first tenant (a synthetic, in-memory token)</label><br>
<input id="token-a" type="text" size="60" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
</p>
<p>
<label for="token-b">Session token of a user of the second tenant</label><br>
<input id="token-b" type="text" size="60" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
</p>
<p><button id="run" type="button">Run every probe</button></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="results-title">
<h2 id="results-title">2. What came back</h2>
<p id="status" role="status">Not run yet. Nothing is shown as isolated until the probes have been answered.</p>
<table>
<caption>One row per probe and per caller</caption>
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">Probe</th><th scope="col">Caller</th><th scope="col">HTTP</th><th scope="col">Outcome</th><th scope="col">Verdict</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody id="rows"></tbody>
</table>
<p id="facts">No facts yet.</p>
</section>
</main>
<script src="/contract.js"></script>
<script src="/page.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
